# Shell scripts and the pod's Python must keep LF endings, whatever the machine
# that edits them.
#
# A CRLF shell script fails in a way that points nowhere useful: a heredoc's
# closing delimiter becomes "PY\r", never matches "PY", and bash reports
# "unexpected end of file" at the last line of the file rather than at the
# heredoc. It cost a launch to find. git's own checkouts were always LF; this
# is for the files that reach a pod by other means -- base64 over ssh, scp, a
# copy-paste -- which bypass the conversion entirely.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
tools/pod text eol=lf
